        "projects_cartas_title": "Letters from the Bottom of the Pit",
        "projects_cartas_desc": "The exhibition reconstructs the history of mining in Rio Grande do Sul through letters and original documents (1891-1964) from the Historical Archive of the State Coal Museum.",
        "projects_school_title": "School at the Museum Project",
        "projects_school_desc": "Educational actions integrated with schools in the Jacuí region, promoting guided visits and educational workshops on the history of mining and environmental preservation.",
        "projects_restoration_title": "Restoration of the CADEM Collection",
        "projects_restoration_desc": "Continuous work of preventive conservation, cleaning, and physical restoration of rare cartographic and manuscript documents from the CADEM archival fund.",
        "projects_btn_learn_more": "Learn More",
        "projects_modal_close": "Close",
        "projects_cartas_modal_title": "Exhibition: Letters from the Bottom of the Pit",
        "projects_cartas_modal_p1": "The exhibition 'Letters from the Bottom of the Pit: Correspondence from the coal mines of Lower Jacuí (1891-1964)' reconstructs key aspects of the social history of mining in Rio Grande do Sul. The exhibited collection consists of a selection of original letters exchanged between workers, mining companies, and their families.",
        "projects_cartas_modal_p2": "<strong>The Jacuí River Basin:</strong> The mines located in the municipalities that make up the Jacuí River Basin, such as Arroio dos Ratos and Butiá, were the core of this rich trajectory. The letters on display depict the painful daily life in the workers' villages, the strong presence of European immigration, and the techniques used in underground coal extraction.",
        "projects_cartas_modal_p3": "<strong>The World War II Effort:</strong> During World War II (1939-1945), mining in Jacuí assumed strategic geopolitical relevance for Brazil. With the international maritime blockade and the scarcity of imported coal from Europe, the mineral extracted in the region became vital to move railroads and feed the thermoelectric plants that sustained Brazilian infrastructure.",
        "projects_cartas_modal_p4": "<strong>Strikes and Social Struggles:</strong> The letters also document tense labor relations, organized strike movements seeking better wages and safety, and the mobilization of miners' unions throughout the 1940s to 1960s.",
        "projects_cartas_modal_info": "<strong>WHERE/WHEN:</strong> Exhibition designed in partnership with the NGO Archivists Without Borders and Surya Projects, originally displayed at the Memorial do Rio Grande do Sul (Porto Alegre). The original documentary collection is under permanent custody and is available for consultation at the Historical Archive of the State Coal Museum, in Arroio dos Ratos/RS.",
        "pubs_hero_title": "Publications and Research",
        "pubs_search_placeholder": "Search publication...",
        "pubs_filter_all_years": "All Years",
        "pubs_btn_download": "Download PDF",
        "pubs_item1_title": "Coal and Steam: The Coal Region in World War II",
        "pubs_item1_author": "Dr. Aloísio Mendes",
        "pubs_item1_desc": "An in-depth analysis of the geopolitical and socioeconomic importance of the Lower Jacuí mines during the Brazilian war effort, highlighting the railway and energy logistics fueled by coal.",
        "pubs_item2_title": "Sources Guide of the Coal Historical Archive",
        "pubs_item2_author": "Prof. Clarissa Werlang",
        "pubs_item2_desc": "An indispensable research instrument for historians and archivists, detailing the taxonomy, subseries, and documentary fonds of ancient mining companies kept by the museum.",
        "pubs_item3_title": "Unionism and Labor Struggle in Arroio dos Ratos (1940-1960)",
        "pubs_item3_author": "Carlos Henrique Silva",
        "pubs_item3_desc": "A sociopolitical study on the miners' strike movements, the structure of the first regional unions, and state repression in the Vargas era and the subsequent democratic period.",
        "pubs_item4_title": "Manual for Preventive Conservation of Railway Documents",
        "pubs_item4_author": "Dr. Beatriz Ramos",
        "pubs_item4_desc": "Practical guidelines applied in the rescue, sanitization, disinfection, and packaging of cartographic and administrative collections exposed to severe weather or climate disasters.",
